\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{A time action on a single spin line}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Let the sole direction act by the identity on
#{S=\mathbb C}. An endomorphism anticommuting with this
direction must vanish, so no spin grading for the
[spinor time map](fdip-017Z) exists. Use a scalar fiber,
ordinary conjugations and trivial links. The positive-sign
choice in \ref{fdip-0184} sends a scalar field to its
conjugate at the reflected site. Its square is the identity.
Time pullback changes the sign of the centered difference
and preserves the neighbor sum. Thus the two terms
of the Wilson operator have opposite transformation signs
whenever both terms are nonzero.}
